CORE
main.py
--unwind 3

^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[python-attribute-error\.\d+\] .*'Obj' object has no attribute 'x' \(AttributeError\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
differential2 §11. A bare-annotation field assigned only conditionally
in __init__ is unbound on the path that skips the assignment; reading
it raises AttributeError. The per-field shadow flag (False at
construction, set True on the instance write) is asserted on reads of
not-definitely-initialized fields, so the flag=False path is detected
path-sensitively rather than reading a silent zero.
